{
  "version": 1,
  "currency": "USD",
  "unit": "per_million_tokens",
  "as_of": "2026-11-12",
  "stale_after_days": 60,
  "notes": [
    "Edit freely or pass your own file with --pricing or PREFIXLENS_PRICING. prefixlens has no prices in its code.",
    "List prices for pay-as-you-go API use, standard tier, global endpoints. Not applied: batch, flex, priority/fast tiers (except Anthropic fast mode, below), data residency or regional uplifts (+10% on several providers), negotiated discounts, and per-modality prices (audio input is priced as text). Subscription plans are not billed per token at all.",
    "Matching: the trace's model id and each name are compared after lowercasing, dropping 'provider/' or 'models/' prefixes, Bedrock region and vendor prefixes and '-v1:0' suffixes, and reading '@' and '.' as '-'. An entry that lists the exact id in names wins; there are no wildcards in this file. A glob 'match' field is still accepted in your own tables and is tried only when no entry names the id.",
    "from/until are inclusive UTC days: a call is priced by the day its request was sent. A model with no entry for a call's day has no price for that call.",
    "when_params selects a price by request parameter: Anthropic fast mode is a request with speed: \"fast\". Fast cache prices are derived from Anthropic's documented multipliers (cache prices stack on the fast input price).",
    "cache_write is the write price for the provider's default lifetime (Anthropic 5 minutes, OpenAI 30 minutes); cache_write_1h is Anthropic's 1-hour write price. cache_write_12h is OpenAI's 12-hour write price, applied to the writes a trace records as 12-hour (usage.cache_write_12h_tokens, trace format 1.2); the rest are priced at cache_write.",
    "tiers apply to a whole request when its prompt (uncached + cache read + cache write) is above above_prompt_tokens. OpenAI's '272K' is read as 272,000 tokens and Gemini's '200k' as 200,000.",
    "cache_ttl_seconds and min_cacheable_tokens on an entry override the provider's for that model; they decide when a miss is called expiry and when a prompt is too short to cache.",
    "families gives cache facts (lifetime, minimum) by model-id prefix, for models no entry lists, such as ones priced from the models.dev catalogue.",
    "exclude lists models left unpriced on purpose, with the reason: they get no price from this table or from the models.dev catalogue.",
    "unverified lists fields not printed on the provider's pages. OpenAI shows no cached-input price ('-') for its pro models; this table charges cached tokens at the input price for them."
  ],
  "sources": {
    "anthropic": {
      "checked": "2026-11-12",
      "urls": [
        "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing",
