        "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/<model>/overview (one page per model)",
        "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching",
        "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/fast-mode",
        "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/model-ids-and-versions",
        "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Every price is on the pricing page and on the model's own page; both agree.",
        "Claude 3.x models are retired and no longer listed, so they have no price here.",
        "Not applied: Batch API (50% off), US-only inference (inference_geo: \"us\", 1.1x on Claude 4.6 and later), Bedrock and Google Cloud prices (set by those platforms; regional endpoints +10%). Their model ids are priced at the first-party list price."
      ]
    },
    "openai": {
      "checked": "2026-11-12",
      "urls": [
        "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing",
        "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/<model> (one page per model)",
        "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-caching",
        "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/fast-mode"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "GPT-5.6 and later charge cache writes (1.25x input for the default 30-minute lifetime, 2.5x for 12 hours) and report them in usage as input_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens; earlier models charge none.",
        "GPT-5.6 Sol's price is promotional until 2026-11-30 and the pages do not state the price after it, so its entry ends that day.",
        "Not applied: Batch and Flex (50% of Standard), Fast (2x; formerly Priority) and Ultrafast (6x). A request's service_tier does not say which tier billed it (Fast requests can be downgraded and billed as Standard, and a project can default to Fast), and traces do not record the response's service_tier.",
        "Models marked shut down are priced from their model pages only; the pricing page no longer lists them. gpt-5-search-api is on the pricing page only. gpt-4o-2024-05-13 is left out: shut down, and historically priced differently from gpt-4o.",
        "Left out: trusted-access and specialised models (cyber, life sciences, legal), image, audio, realtime and embedding models."
      ]
    },
    "gemini": {
      "checked": "2026-11-12",
      "urls": [
        "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing",
        "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models",
        "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/caching",
        "https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/pricing (cross-check of the global-endpoint prices)"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The 'context caching price' is the price of cached input tokens, for implicit hits and explicit caches alike. Explicit-cache storage ($ per million tokens per hour) is not applied: traces do not record how long a cache was stored. Gemini 4 models support implicit caching only.",
        "Gemini 4 and 3.6/3.8 Flash prices are promotional until the dates given and double after them; both periods are listed.",
        "gemini-2.5-pro calls from 2026-12-01 are routed to gemini-3.8-flash and billed at its rates; gemini-2.5-flash calls from 2026-12-01 are billed at gemini-3.5-flash-lite rates, which are the same as its own.",
        "Text, image and video input prices are used; audio input costs more on several models and is not told apart.",
        "Not applied: Batch and Flex (50%), Priority. 'latest' aliases such as gemini-flash-latest are listed in exclude: Google hot-swaps the model behind them.",
        "Gemini 3 Flash Preview's $3.00 output price is on the Gemini API pricing page; the Google Cloud page does not show that row."
      ]
    }
  },
